---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Kicker from '../components/content/Kicker.astro';

const title = 'Terms | PainToBuild';
const description = 'Sales terms, refund policy, and the limits of what a PainToBuild analysis or Focused Analysis engagement can promise.';
const lastReviewed = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="wrap section prose">
    <Kicker>Legal</Kicker>
    <h1>Terms</h1>

    <h2>What's sold here</h2>
    <p>
      Two things: the $19 Builder Validation Brief, a digital file, and Focused Analysis, a
      written service engagement. Both are sold and processed through Gumroad, which is the
      merchant of record for every transaction on this site. PainToBuild does not invoice or
      process payment directly for anything.
    </p>

    <h2>Refunds</h2>
    <p>
      The Brief is a digital product delivered instantly on purchase; as with most instant-download
      files, sales are final and not refundable except where required by law or at Gumroad's own
      buyer-protection discretion. Focused Analysis follows the same no-refund policy once work has
      started on your specific material; if you cancel before any work begins, you'll be refunded
      in full.
    </p>

    <h2>What an analysis is, and isn't</h2>
    <p>
      Every page on this site, and every Focused Analysis engagement, is research opinion applied
      consistently through a published methodology. It is not a guarantee of any outcome. Recurring
      pain in the evidence is not proof that a product will sell, and a build/change/watch/stop
      recommendation is a read on the evidence available at the time, not a promise about what
      will happen if you follow it.
    </p>

    <h2>Accuracy</h2>
    <p>
      Sources are verified and dated at the time each page is published. Public conversations get
      deleted, edited, or go stale; if you spot something that's changed or was mis-cited,
      <a href="/contact/">tell us</a> and it will be corrected.
    </p>

    <h2>Who you're dealing with</h2>
    <p>
      PainToBuild is operated under a pseudonym, deliberately kept separate from the operator's
      unrelated professional work. See <a href="/about/">About</a> for why. Because Gumroad is
      the merchant of record for every purchase on this site, no separate legal identity needs to
      appear here for you to have a real seller of record, buyer protections, and a receipt.
    </p>

    <p class="note">Last reviewed {lastReviewed}.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .section { padding-block: var(--s7) var(--s8); }
  .note { color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--t-caption); }
</style>
